course: dictionary
lesson: 5410
title: A laboratory is a place to test ideas
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A laboratory is a room or building with special equipment, where scientists do experiments and tests. Your school science room can be a lab too, where you wear goggles and follow safety rules while you test ideas.
explain: Use the words around a new word to find its meaning. «The International Space Station is a big laboratory orbiting Earth with astronauts on board.» Orbiting Earth and astronauts on board are clues that a laboratory can be far above the ground, not only in a school. Ask yourself: what word would fit here? A place where scientists work and test things.
explain: People often shorten laboratory to lab, as in «the lab». Madagascar is called «a laboratory of the strange», so the word can also mean a place full of things scientists find strange and interesting. Check your meaning by putting it into the sentence in place of the hard word: if it still makes sense, you are right.
fact: A laboratory is a room or building with special equipment for experiments and tests.
fact: The short form of laboratory is lab, and people say «the lab» much more often than the full word.
fact: «Sodium metal reacts with air within seconds, so laboratories keep it under oil.»
fact: «There are 118 known elements; about 90 are found in nature and the rest were made in laboratories.»
fact: «The International Space Station is a big laboratory orbiting Earth» and it goes around the Earth about every 90 minutes.
exercise: «The International Space Station is a big laboratory orbiting Earth.» What is a laboratory in this sentence? | *A room or building with special equipment for experiments | A large garden with rare plants | A school playground | A kind of spaceship that carries food
exercise: «Sodium metal reacts with air within seconds, so laboratories keep it under oil.» Why do laboratories keep sodium under oil? | Because oil keeps it warm | *Because it reacts quickly with air | Because oil makes it taste better | Because it is too heavy to lift
exercise: Nadia says, «We have science in the lab today.» Find and copy the short form of laboratory. | have | science | *lab | today
test: «Madagascar is a laboratory of the strange.» What does this suggest? | A place with no animals at all | A very cold place with snow all year | A shop that sells toys | *A place full of strange and unusual creatures
test: Before her experiment, Nadia puts on a lab coat. What is a lab coat for? | For swimming in the pool | To look smart at parties | *To protect your clothes during experiments | To keep you warm outdoors
exam: «There are 118 known elements; about 90 are found in nature and the rest were made in laboratories.» About how many elements were made in laboratories? | About 118 | *About 28 | None at all | About 90
